  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Thus, the graph of the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is given by</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c7558290-8216-415d-8bf2-18cc853de6c2-image.png\" style=\"width: 315px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>If a line parallel to the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis intersects the graph of a function at more than one point, then the function is many-one.</p><p>And, it is clear from the graph that, the given function is many-one.</p><p>Also, the range of the function is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;which is not same as the co-domain which is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and if the co-domain of a function and range are not same then the function is not onto.</p><p>Hence, the given function is neither one-one nor onto.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
